+// The relay child's side of enclave-derived-commit/v1 (logs/derived-state-ipc-contract.md; KVM API per
+// logs/image-enrollment-root-note.txt): durable derived-reader state is committed by the platform-api ROLE (the parent) to its
+// replica majority, over the private child IPC channel, and only the role's exact, bound reply counts. No HTTP answer, queued
+// message or local write is durability. The enrollment KVM's enrollDerivedState needs comes from the role the same way.
+//   createDerivedCommitter({ boot }) -> {
+//     commit({ file, bytes, sha256, signal }) -> Promise<true>          (KVM options.journalCommit / openLifecycleJournal commit)
+//     verifyEnrollment({ binding, floorDigest, signal }) -> Promise<result>  (KVM enrollDerivedState verifyEnrollment)
+//     status() }
+// A request resolves ONLY for a reply naming this boot and this request id, echoing its subject (the bytes' sha256; the
+// binding and floor digest), ok, and well formed. Anything else - a timeout, a refusal, a mismatched echo, an abort while in
+// flight, a closed channel - FENCES the committer: every later request rejects (derived_commit_fenced) for the life of this
+// process. Requests are serialized (one in flight); a late or unknown reply resolves nothing.
+import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
